WEBVTT

00:10.870 --> 00:12.240
Is this the right place?

00:13.040 --> 00:15.910
Taishi said he'd take care of everything, but...

00:20.480 --> 00:22.970
You and I together are "Brother 2"!

00:25.050 --> 00:27.350
Is your flame burning?!

00:27.590 --> 00:29.420
Is your heart singing?!

00:29.890 --> 00:31.120
Comrade Kazuki!

00:33.630 --> 00:36.060
What the heck is this "Brother 2"?

00:36.330 --> 00:39.820
Why, it's the name of our group, of course!

00:42.730 --> 00:45.230
That is the battleground of "Brother 2"!

00:45.500 --> 00:47.210
On this day, Kazuki Sendou will become...

00:47.210 --> 00:49.940
...the fearless tiger of the exhibition and spot sale!

00:49.940 --> 00:51.880
You mean shopboy, right?

00:51.940 --> 00:53.970
No!

00:54.180 --> 00:55.940
Lukewarm! Far too lukewarm!

00:56.680 --> 00:59.450
An exhibition and spot sale is a head-on battle between buyers and sellers!

00:59.550 --> 01:01.380
It is a coliseum of paper!

01:01.550 --> 01:04.550
Listen well! This is the one-way ticket there!

01:04.920 --> 01:07.190
Participant Registration Card

01:04.920 --> 01:07.190
Group Name: Brother 2

01:04.920 --> 01:07.190
Group Representative: Kazuki Sendou

01:07.830 --> 01:10.960
"Admission of groups is 8-9AM."

01:10.960 --> 01:12.590
"Times are strictly observed."

01:13.160 --> 01:14.930
Rule number one of exhibition and spot sales!

01:15.730 --> 01:18.000
Come what may, tardiness is absolutely taboo.

01:18.270 --> 01:20.800
You cannot sell anything unless you get inside the convention hall.

01:21.140 --> 01:26.080
In other words, a virtual death for any participant!

01:27.780 --> 01:29.050
Run! Run!

01:29.050 --> 01:30.450
Say that first! First, okay?!

01:30.450 --> 01:32.380
Come on, come on, hurry!

01:35.320 --> 01:38.880
<i>Just be you and don't change.</i>
<i>Kimi no Mama de Kawaranaide</i>

01:39.390 --> 01:42.530
<i>You're more precious to me than anyone.</i>
<i>Dare Yori mo Taisetsu na</i>

01:42.530 --> 01:46.090
<i>You have a great, sparkling dream...</i>
<i>Ohki na Yume Kagayakaseta</i>

01:46.330 --> 01:49.360
<i>...and you're my one and only friend.</i>
<i>Tada Hitori no Tomodachi</i>

01:49.630 --> 01:53.270
<i>It just doesn't get across...</i>
<i>Nani o Shite mo Tsutawarazu</i>

01:53.270 --> 01:56.840
<i>It's just not working right at all.</i>
<i>Umaku Ikanai Bakari de</i>

01:56.840 --> 02:00.180
<i>But even I and everyone else...</i>
<i>Watashi Datte Dare Datte</i>

02:00.410 --> 02:03.910
<i>... have times like that.</i>
<i>Atarimae ni Aru Koto</i>

02:04.020 --> 02:07.380
<i>Those things that don't return to your heart.</i>
<i>Mune no Naka ni Kaeranai</i>

02:07.590 --> 02:10.990
<i>But even those words and feelings...</i>
<i>Omoi mo Kotoba mo Itsuka</i>

02:11.160 --> 02:15.560
<i>... will come back in time someday...</i>
<i>Jikan ga Tateba Modotte Kuru kara</i>

02:15.790 --> 02:18.700
<i>... before you know it.</i>
<i>Shiranai Uchi ni</i>

02:19.000 --> 02:24.940
<i>There's only one thing you can do right now.</i>
<i>Ima Kimiga Dekiru Koto wa Hitotsu</i>

02:25.270 --> 02:32.010
<i>Just accept it and go with it.</i>
<i>Sono Mama Ukeirete Yukou</i>

02:32.640 --> 02:36.650
<i>Just be you and stay true to yourself.</i>
<i>Kimi no Mama de Itsuwarazu ni</i>

02:36.650 --> 02:39.820
<i>Take a little break.</i>
<i>Sukoshi Hitoyasumi Shite</i>

02:39.820 --> 02:43.590
<i>Take your impatience and your hardships...</i>
<i>Aseru Kimochi Kurushii Koto</i>

02:43.590 --> 02:46.850
<i>...and turn them into your strengths.</i>
<i>Kimi no Power ni Kaete</i>

02:46.930 --> 02:50.690
<i>Just be you and don't change.</i>
<i>Kimi no Mama de Kawaranaide</i>

02:51.030 --> 02:54.170
<i>You're more precious to me than anyone.</i>
<i>Dare Yori mo Taisetsu na</i>

02:54.170 --> 02:57.760
<i>You have a great, sparkling dream...</i>
<i>Ohki na Yume Kagayakaseta</i>

02:57.940 --> 03:00.870
<i>...and you're my one and only friend.</i>
<i>Tada Hitori no Tomodachi</i>

03:03.880 --> 03:10.680
BUYERS, SELLERS,

03:03.880 --> 03:10.680
EXHIBITION

03:03.880 --> 03:10.680
AND SPOT SALE

03:16.750 --> 03:18.090
Sorry!

03:18.560 --> 03:20.330
Sheesh! You're late, Mizuki!

03:20.330 --> 03:22.060
Sorry, sorry, I'll treat you to tea.

03:22.190 --> 03:23.680
In that case, I forgive you.

03:27.130 --> 03:28.100
Where do you want to start?

03:28.100 --> 03:29.570
Oh, I want a pair of mules.

03:36.140 --> 03:37.140
"Convention Hall"

03:37.140 --> 03:39.100
"Group Registration"

03:37.440 --> 03:39.100
Pardon me! Coming through!

03:39.410 --> 03:41.500
Please submit your sample issues!

03:42.550 --> 03:44.070
Their enthusiasm is amazing.

03:44.280 --> 03:46.350
Let's see, where am I supposed to go?

03:46.350 --> 03:47.250
Hey, Taishi...?

03:47.620 --> 03:48.380
Huh?

03:51.920 --> 03:53.260
Forgive me, my brother.

03:53.590 --> 03:56.130
They say a lion exerts his utmost even to fell a rabbit,

03:56.130 --> 03:58.530
and that he thrusts his own children down an abyss...

03:58.530 --> 04:01.190
...only to further kick sand upon them.

04:01.800 --> 04:04.570
I, too, send you into the exhibition and spot sale alone,

04:04.570 --> 04:06.270
though it rends my heart to do so.

04:06.500 --> 04:08.500
Climb back up victorious.

04:08.570 --> 04:10.510
"200 yen"

04:14.680 --> 04:15.700
Participant Registration Card 12

04:14.680 --> 04:15.700
Receipt Number: 12-0682

04:14.680 --> 04:15.700
Location: F-01B

04:14.680 --> 04:15.700
Group Name: Brother 2

04:17.320 --> 04:18.840
Um, excuse me...

04:19.320 --> 04:20.010
What?

04:20.080 --> 04:22.610
Is this F-01-B?

04:24.520 --> 04:25.220
Y-yes...

04:26.260 --> 04:29.890
Um, I'm Kazuki Sendou.
Nice to meet you.

04:31.430 --> 04:32.900
I am Aya Hasebe.

04:40.370 --> 04:42.470
Hey, there's no standing sign.
Who's in charge?

04:42.610 --> 04:44.100
Over here, over here.

04:45.910 --> 04:49.450
I'm sorry, it's my first time at an exhibition and spot sale,

04:49.450 --> 04:51.250
but is it always like this?

04:51.520 --> 04:52.180
What?

04:52.180 --> 04:53.980
Have you been doing this for long?

04:54.750 --> 04:55.450
Yes...

04:57.960 --> 05:00.790
Um... your books certainly arrived early.

05:00.490 --> 05:01.190
What?

05:01.930 --> 05:04.950
I placed my order at a place called Tsukamoto Printers.

05:05.100 --> 05:07.700
It's small, but I heard that they do a thorough job, so...

05:07.700 --> 05:10.300
<i>"Brother 2", your delivery has arrived.</i>

05:10.300 --> 05:13.100
<i>Please immediately go to the</i>

05:10.300 --> 05:13.100
<i>loading dock to receive it.</i>

05:10.940 --> 05:14.470
Still, they're so late. It looks like it's going to start soon...

05:15.140 --> 05:16.040
No...

05:16.270 --> 05:17.040
Huh?

05:17.910 --> 05:19.680
You have to go get it yourself here.

05:18.740 --> 05:23.240
<i>"Brother 2", please come immediately</i>

05:18.740 --> 05:23.240
<i>and pick up your delivery.</i>

05:23.720 --> 05:25.080
That's me!

05:31.390 --> 05:33.260
Rule number two of exhibition and spot sales.

05:33.630 --> 05:35.660
The doujinshi comes first and foremost.

05:35.660 --> 05:38.720
You must obtain your books as soon as you get to the convention hall.

05:39.130 --> 05:40.390
LOADING DOCK

05:40.670 --> 05:42.360
Oh, I'm so sorry!

05:42.870 --> 05:44.360
Oh, Sir!

05:49.210 --> 05:50.580
Thank goodness.

05:50.580 --> 05:53.550
I was getting worried about what might have happened to you.

05:53.880 --> 05:56.810
Sorry, sorry, this is my first time, so I don't know my way around.

05:57.150 --> 05:59.120
Here it is. Please take it.

05:59.120 --> 06:00.050
Thank you.

06:00.220 --> 06:00.990
Sir!

06:00.990 --> 06:01.680
What?

06:01.890 --> 06:05.850
It has been a while since I have enjoyed printing a book this much.

06:06.120 --> 06:08.260
Mr. Machine never once became unhappy...

06:08.260 --> 06:10.920
...and both Mr. Paper and Mr. Ink were smiling happily.

06:11.400 --> 06:12.920
Good luck, please.

06:14.600 --> 06:15.460
Thank you.

06:21.340 --> 06:23.400
Rule number three of exhibition and spot sales.

06:23.780 --> 06:26.870
Never forget to submit a sample copy to the administrators.

06:27.210 --> 06:28.580
I'm sorry.

06:28.780 --> 06:29.610
Thank you so much.

06:31.250 --> 06:34.820
Depending on the content, they may order you to halt sales.

06:34.820 --> 06:36.220
Perilous, perilous.

06:38.790 --> 06:41.950
Wow! So, this is my book!

06:43.730 --> 06:46.290
It's really been printed! Awesome!

06:59.110 --> 07:02.570
<i>Comic Bravo is now open!</i>

07:03.210 --> 07:04.910
All right! I'm going to sell!

07:05.720 --> 07:07.310
Please enter without running!

07:10.760 --> 07:12.380
Hey, which do you like?

07:12.990 --> 07:14.790
Hmm, let me think...

07:15.190 --> 07:16.590
Guess I'll just buy both!

07:16.590 --> 07:18.500
Ooh, you rich girl, you!

07:18.830 --> 07:21.430
Well, I haven't been out like this in a while.

07:23.530 --> 07:25.330
All right! I'm going to buy!

07:25.770 --> 07:27.910
Will you take a ske-boo request?

07:27.910 --> 07:29.510
Here's a little something to eat.

07:29.510 --> 07:31.670
I've been looking forward to your new volume!

07:36.950 --> 07:37.880
I see.

07:38.350 --> 07:39.340
Soon.

07:40.590 --> 07:41.420
All right!

07:55.600 --> 07:58.130
Maybe people prefer those kinds of books in the end.

08:04.380 --> 08:06.940
O-our place alone is kind of quiet, isn't it?

08:09.350 --> 08:10.180
Oh! No!

08:10.250 --> 08:13.280
I didn't mean to imply that it's not selling or that it's not popular!

08:13.450 --> 08:17.080
That's true for me, but um, that's not the case for you...

08:18.560 --> 08:20.460
There's some space here.

08:20.460 --> 08:22.290
I guess that makes one round.

08:22.730 --> 08:25.100
The crop of maid stories was pretty poor.

08:25.100 --> 08:28.500
That's over already.
Next is certain to be angel stories.

08:32.700 --> 08:34.540
Or drill mecha, though that's a long shot.

08:34.870 --> 08:37.770
Personally, wings don't really appeal to me.

08:38.440 --> 08:41.450
The quality of Comi-Bra has dropped lately.

08:41.450 --> 08:45.450
But I got the new volume from "Cat or Fish", so it's not so bad.

08:45.450 --> 08:48.420
This year's Comi-Bra is low quality.

08:49.050 --> 08:49.950
E-excuse me...

08:50.390 --> 08:52.690
Trying to sell to us?

08:53.390 --> 08:55.490
No, your bottle!

08:54.190 --> 08:55.490
Let's see.

08:55.490 --> 08:56.980
Oh, one of these.

09:02.730 --> 09:04.530
This is no, no good.

09:06.000 --> 09:08.670
The characters don't stand out, and it is not very gripping.

09:08.670 --> 09:10.400
What kind of story is this?

09:10.840 --> 09:13.780
What current readers are seeking are romantic comedies.

09:15.210 --> 09:18.240
You should study up on the books by the major players.

09:18.350 --> 09:19.980
That way, you might...

09:20.350 --> 09:21.820
How rude is that?!

09:21.820 --> 09:23.590
You're the rude one.

09:23.590 --> 09:26.120
It's very bad to pick a fight with your readers.

09:26.120 --> 09:29.360
We only gave you frank and constructive advice.

09:29.360 --> 09:31.850
That is not what I'm talking about! First of all...

09:35.630 --> 09:36.270
I'm so sorry!

09:36.270 --> 09:37.260
Are you okay?

09:37.540 --> 09:39.770
As this is not our responsibility...

09:39.770 --> 09:41.930
That's right, it's got nothing to do with us.

09:42.410 --> 09:45.410
Um, I'll watch the table, so please go to the restroom...

09:45.410 --> 09:45.940
What?

09:45.940 --> 09:47.680
I'll keep proper watch in your absence,

09:47.680 --> 09:49.010
so please go get the stain out.

09:49.080 --> 09:50.740
Thank you. In that case...

09:56.790 --> 09:57.980
I'm so bad...

10:01.760 --> 10:04.350
<i>I got so riled up over such a small thing.</i>

10:08.900 --> 10:11.060
The way of the doujin is a path of briars.

10:11.200 --> 10:12.870
Endure and survive, Kazuki!

10:12.000 --> 10:14.860
It's so super-empty here! That's so lame!

10:18.140 --> 10:19.540
Isn't that Eimi Ohba?

10:19.210 --> 10:21.450
She sold out first in the morning, right?

10:21.250 --> 10:23.610
Why is she in the original genre area?

10:24.850 --> 10:26.920
You're still selling? Poor guy.

10:26.920 --> 10:27.850
You're...

10:27.850 --> 10:30.250
I sold out in one hour.

10:30.790 --> 10:34.160
Hmm, so this is the sort of thing you draw.

10:37.190 --> 10:38.430
Ta-da!

10:37.830 --> 10:38.430
"A Girl's Feelings"

10:38.430 --> 10:39.490
I'll trade you!

10:39.960 --> 10:41.990
It's the new issue from "Cat or Fish"!

10:42.130 --> 10:43.690
Who's that? He's so lucky!

10:44.770 --> 10:45.800
What? That's okay, really.

10:45.800 --> 10:47.860
Wh-what did you say?!

10:48.110 --> 10:49.700
That is super-unbelievable!

10:49.940 --> 10:52.740
It's the great, cute
Eimi Ohba's newest issue!

10:52.810 --> 10:57.440
It's super-popular, sold out super-right away, and super-awesome!

10:58.220 --> 11:00.080
Then rather than have someone like me read it...

11:00.250 --> 11:03.390
You can't buy it even if you line up sometimes, and I'm giving it to you!

11:03.390 --> 11:06.260
There, you want it now, don't you?
You want it, right?!

11:06.260 --> 11:07.950
I'm telling you, it's okay...

11:09.930 --> 11:12.560
You can just keep drawing quack sober, sober doujinshi...

11:12.560 --> 11:13.830
...for the rest of your life for all I care!

11:14.830 --> 11:16.430
That's my business, not yours!

11:16.430 --> 11:18.770
Humph! You only have that many copies?!

11:18.770 --> 11:21.200
I sold ten full cardboard boxes worth! Ten!

11:21.610 --> 11:24.740
I might have fewer copies, but it could still be a good book!

11:24.740 --> 11:26.040
You don't get it!

11:26.040 --> 11:28.010
Doujinshi that don't sell are no good!

11:28.010 --> 11:29.610
If it's not popular, it's trash!

11:29.850 --> 11:33.440
Doujinshi that no one reads is just super-sad!

11:34.120 --> 11:36.750
Well? Do you understand what the great, cute Eimi is saying?

11:36.750 --> 11:38.290
No, not at all!

11:38.290 --> 11:38.660
Wha...

11:38.660 --> 11:41.320
That's right, that's right, as if anyone would understand.

11:55.110 --> 11:56.770
I brought ya a little somethin' to eat.

11:56.770 --> 11:57.810
Knowin' you,

11:57.810 --> 12:00.610
you haven't brought anythin' to put in your stomach, have you?

12:00.610 --> 12:01.580
Oh, yeah...

12:01.680 --> 12:06.080
I hate how lately, there's a lot more people who've got the wrong idea.

12:06.080 --> 12:08.120
They think they're somehow better 'cause they sell more issues

12:08.120 --> 12:09.390
and people line up for their stuff.

12:09.390 --> 12:11.880
If you've got no love for doujin, just quit. That's what I say.

12:11.990 --> 12:15.430
If your sales are that important, then go professional!

12:15.590 --> 12:16.250
Right?

12:16.490 --> 12:18.200
Wh-what are you looking at me for?

12:18.200 --> 12:19.730
What do you mean by that?!

12:19.260 --> 12:20.320
Nothin'.

12:22.470 --> 12:24.370
Now now, don't go gettin' your panties in a bunch.

12:24.370 --> 12:27.130
Have a fried noodle bread and cheer up.

12:28.310 --> 12:31.180
I don't want it! This is why
I hate the country panda!

12:31.180 --> 12:32.880
I'm super-pissed, so I'm going home!

12:32.880 --> 12:34.740
Oh, so sorry to see you go.

12:36.580 --> 12:38.620
If you don't like what I said, then sell at least one copy!

12:38.620 --> 12:41.640
If you can't sell any, you're just a mutt howling from a distance!

12:44.290 --> 12:45.420
See ya.

12:46.960 --> 12:47.860
There you have it.

12:48.390 --> 12:49.160
Thanks.

12:49.230 --> 12:50.630
I'll let you in on a little secret.

12:50.630 --> 12:53.690
Eimi Ohba can't stand stuff with green laver on them.

12:53.830 --> 12:55.090
Green laver?

12:55.730 --> 12:58.430
Like octopus balls, fried noodles, and Japanese pizza.

12:58.800 --> 13:01.640
I think it was 'round when she got popular enough to get a wall space,

13:01.640 --> 13:03.230
right when she started throwin' her weight around.

13:03.470 --> 13:05.640
She had green laver stuck in her teeth and people saw it.

13:05.640 --> 13:07.080
She's been traumatized ever since.

13:07.480 --> 13:08.170
I see...

13:08.680 --> 13:11.210
I'm glad I bought it, just in case somethin' like this came up.

13:11.420 --> 13:14.040
There's nothin' like fried noodle bread to shoo Eimi away.

13:14.520 --> 13:17.010
Well, I wouldn't recommend it for an ordinary snack, though.

13:17.090 --> 13:20.020
You should avoid stuff that spoils easily, like ones with cream in 'em.

13:20.020 --> 13:22.760
You gotta think about these things, even if they're just snacks.

13:23.330 --> 13:26.730
Um, thank you very much.

13:28.600 --> 13:30.970
Oh, she's the group sitting next to me.

13:31.370 --> 13:33.960
Just now, I actually accidentally spilled cola...

13:36.910 --> 13:38.400
You sure bought a lot.

13:39.440 --> 13:41.340
So, what happened this time?

13:41.480 --> 13:42.910
What do you mean?

13:42.910 --> 13:44.520
Well, it's your usual pattern.

13:44.520 --> 13:46.480
When something happens, you go on a shopping spree.

13:46.480 --> 13:48.390
N-nothing happened.

13:48.390 --> 13:50.990
There were just a lot of things I wanted to buy!

13:50.990 --> 13:52.890
Really?

13:52.890 --> 13:54.720
Never mind that, where should we go next?

13:56.160 --> 13:57.860
Oh, a movie sounds good...

13:57.860 --> 14:00.200
I'm sorry, I've got stuff I have to do after this.

14:01.470 --> 14:03.370
Let's go to a movie next time.

14:03.370 --> 14:04.560
I'll keep you company, okay?

14:04.640 --> 14:07.500
Don't worry, I'm perfectly capable of going to the movies alone.

14:12.510 --> 14:14.110
Well, no wonder!

14:14.110 --> 14:14.770
What?

14:14.950 --> 14:18.250
I'm sayin' you can't complain if people think this table is a no-show.

14:18.250 --> 14:20.220
What's with this plain table?

14:20.950 --> 14:23.820
It's really hard for me to tell if you wanna sell or not.

14:24.960 --> 14:28.150
You said books can be good, even with very few copies, right?

14:28.360 --> 14:28.960
Yeah.

14:28.960 --> 14:31.400
But you gotta first get people to take a look at 'em...

14:31.400 --> 14:33.420
...for them to find out if it's interestin' or not!

14:34.700 --> 14:36.760
Rule number four of exhibition and spot sales.

14:37.540 --> 14:39.300
Setting up your space is the most vital task,

14:39.300 --> 14:40.870
which will directly affect your sales.

14:40.870 --> 14:42.130
Good of you to notice it.

14:45.540 --> 14:47.310
It just isn't eyecatchin'.

14:47.480 --> 14:49.910
There's nothin' you can do about only havin' one kind of book,

14:49.910 --> 14:51.550
but you don't even have the price listed.

14:51.550 --> 14:52.880
How much are ya gonna sell it for?!

14:53.050 --> 14:54.820
What? Price? Um...

14:54.820 --> 14:57.810
The sellin' point of your work.
What's exciting about your work.

14:58.020 --> 14:59.960
You gotta display those things.

15:00.090 --> 15:00.690
Okay.

15:00.690 --> 15:02.360
I thought somethin' like this might happen,

15:02.360 --> 15:04.290
so I came prepared!

15:04.900 --> 15:06.260
Ta-da!

15:07.830 --> 15:09.800
Limited edition, 50 copies!
Extremely rare item!

15:08.070 --> 15:09.800
"Limited edition,

15:08.070 --> 15:09.800
50 copies!

15:08.070 --> 15:09.800
Extremely

15:08.070 --> 15:09.800
rare item!"

15:09.870 --> 15:13.800
Currently duking it out with Eimi
Ohba. Kazuki Sendou's shop!

15:10.130 --> 15:13.800
"Currently duking it out

15:10.130 --> 15:13.800
with Eimi Ohba.

15:10.130 --> 15:13.800
Kazuki Sendou's shop!"

15:17.340 --> 15:18.430
How's that?!

15:19.110 --> 15:21.410
I-I sort of feel like an actor, whose popularity is waning.

15:21.410 --> 15:23.980
Who cares?! It's okay as long as it's appealing!

15:23.980 --> 15:26.350
Now, all you need is a bright and lively hawkin'.

15:26.350 --> 15:27.380
Come on, you too!

15:27.380 --> 15:29.250
It doesn't matter if they only read it without buying,

15:29.250 --> 15:30.380
you win if you can get them to pick it up!

15:30.720 --> 15:31.450
O-okay.

15:31.520 --> 15:32.580
All right!

15:33.060 --> 15:35.430
Come on, come on, gather 'round! Have a look!

15:35.430 --> 15:38.000
That's enough, I'll do the rest myself.

15:38.000 --> 15:38.860
Oh, yeah?

15:38.860 --> 15:40.260
Yeah, thanks, okay?

15:40.830 --> 15:43.320
Then I'll go look around the hall.

15:45.070 --> 15:46.160
What you said.

15:47.570 --> 15:50.670
It's still a doujinshi, whether it's a parody or an original...

15:50.670 --> 15:52.910
...and whether you sell four copies or ten.

15:53.110 --> 15:55.640
Eimi just doesn't quite get it.

15:55.780 --> 15:58.540
Well, it looks like you realized it, so it's okay.

15:59.680 --> 16:00.650
Good luck!

16:07.190 --> 16:09.720
Bright and lively hawking, huh?

16:11.760 --> 16:15.390
Please, come read my book!
It's an original action work!

16:15.600 --> 16:19.000
Teasing is perfectly welcome!
Please feel free to come read it!

16:19.000 --> 16:21.000
"Shooting Star in Love"

16:32.950 --> 16:35.390
Go right ahead!
Feel free to read it through!

16:35.390 --> 16:36.690
Please have a look at it!

16:36.690 --> 16:38.120
It's sure to entertain you!

16:38.120 --> 16:39.690
Feel free to read it through!

16:39.390 --> 16:41.490
Excuse me.

16:39.690 --> 16:41.490
It's sure to entertain you!

16:41.660 --> 16:43.160
How much is it?

16:43.160 --> 16:44.250
How much?

16:46.000 --> 16:47.560
The price of this book.

16:47.800 --> 16:49.960
What? Book...? How much...?

16:50.630 --> 16:52.600
You're going to buy it?! You?! Really?!

16:52.600 --> 16:53.840
How much is it?

16:53.840 --> 16:57.210
Oh, price, right. Price, price, um...

16:57.210 --> 16:59.040
Sorry, I haven't decided yet.

16:59.040 --> 17:00.740
How much should I sell it for?

17:01.150 --> 17:03.810
A thousand yen? That's expensive, right? A hundred yen?

17:03.810 --> 17:06.220
That's too cheap, um, um...

17:07.320 --> 17:10.410
Well...uh, um...
I-I-I'll give it to you, as a gift!

17:11.260 --> 17:13.120
You're my first customer, so it's free!

17:13.120 --> 17:14.460
You can't do that!

17:14.660 --> 17:15.390
What?

17:15.630 --> 17:17.220
Would 500 yen be all right?

17:17.800 --> 17:18.850
Oh, sure, that's okay.

17:19.130 --> 17:19.960
Then, here you go.

17:20.400 --> 17:21.090
O-okay.

17:21.170 --> 17:22.000
Goodbye.

17:25.270 --> 17:26.070
I sold it...

17:26.400 --> 17:28.900
One of my books sold for the first time.

17:31.110 --> 17:32.510
Th-thank you.

17:36.480 --> 17:39.350
I wasn't even able to thank her.
What the heck am I doing?

17:39.350 --> 17:43.050
Excuse me. May I take a look at it?

17:43.690 --> 17:44.590
G-go right ahead.

17:50.690 --> 17:51.460
I'll take it.

17:52.500 --> 17:53.560
Th-thank you very much.

17:53.630 --> 17:55.060
Would you sign it for me?

17:55.530 --> 17:56.330
S-sign?

17:56.870 --> 17:58.630
Uh, p-please wait a minute.

17:59.070 --> 17:59.900
Um...

18:01.170 --> 18:02.010
Th-thanks.

18:02.010 --> 18:04.410
I'll make sure to check out your work from now on.

18:04.640 --> 18:08.810
What? Uh, ch-check out...
Thank you very much.

18:15.790 --> 18:17.810
Rule number five of exhibition and spot sales.

18:18.560 --> 18:21.130
Yes, this is the most important thing.

18:21.130 --> 18:23.460
Never forget that feeling of gratitude.

18:24.030 --> 18:26.530
<i>The time is four o'clock</i> <i>in the afternoon...</i>

18:26.530 --> 18:29.400
<i>...and Comic Bravo will now be closing.</i>

18:31.240 --> 18:32.360
It's over.

18:32.970 --> 18:37.030
<i>All groups, please clean up by five o'clock.</i>

18:37.470 --> 18:41.540
Eight copies.
Of which one was a sample copy.

18:42.580 --> 18:46.380
But there are seven people out there who'll read my comic.

18:46.850 --> 18:47.820
Mr. Sendou.

18:48.620 --> 18:49.310
Y-yes!

18:49.450 --> 18:51.920
Thank you for everything today.

18:51.920 --> 18:53.620
Not at all!

18:54.020 --> 18:56.290
I was the one who seemed to have caused you all the trouble.

18:56.290 --> 19:00.160
Not at all... If you're interested, would you read my book?

19:00.160 --> 19:01.930
What? Are you sure?

19:02.730 --> 19:03.360
Yes.

19:04.600 --> 19:05.830
Thank you so much!

19:07.540 --> 19:10.170
Um, then, please take one of mine.

19:10.310 --> 19:11.780
Thank you very much.

19:12.780 --> 19:14.680
I had fun today.

19:16.650 --> 19:17.980
Y-yes, see you again.

19:28.960 --> 19:30.450
It was fun.

19:30.990 --> 19:33.690
I was able to complete my doujinshi debut without mishap.

19:36.570 --> 19:37.870
Considering the typical pattern,

19:37.870 --> 19:40.000
Taishi should suddenly show up about now...

19:40.600 --> 19:42.130
"Pinwheel"

19:44.880 --> 19:46.740
Her name was Miss Hasebe, wasn't it?

19:46.940 --> 19:49.050
She had quite a bit of stuff with her, too.

19:49.050 --> 19:50.780
I wonder if she didn't sell too many?

19:51.250 --> 19:53.770
I guess it is a bit on the plain side, like the cover...

19:56.620 --> 19:58.990
The art style sort of has a warm feel to it...

20:29.120 --> 20:30.280
Wow...

20:31.050 --> 20:32.260
She's amazing!

20:32.260 --> 20:34.230
I had no idea she could draw something so interesting.

20:34.690 --> 20:36.860
Doujinshi that don't sell are no good!

20:36.860 --> 20:38.560
If it's not popular, it's trash!

20:38.560 --> 20:41.530
Doujinshi that no one reads are just super-sad!

20:42.570 --> 20:44.660
She's right, it is sad.

20:45.170 --> 20:47.800
But that doesn't mean it's trash.

20:48.370 --> 20:50.970
I'm gonna keep on drawing what I like after all.

20:52.410 --> 20:54.310
I've got a long way to go.

20:54.850 --> 20:56.250
Compared to Miss Hasebe,

20:56.250 --> 20:58.850
my story is self-complacent and the finish is rough.

20:58.850 --> 21:00.720
I've gotta work on every aspect of it.

21:01.590 --> 21:02.720
I'd better work hard.

21:02.720 --> 21:04.020
Bravo!

21:08.860 --> 21:11.230
It seems you have made it through this day without mishap,

21:11.230 --> 21:12.090
my brother.

21:12.630 --> 21:13.360
You...

21:13.900 --> 21:15.370
Buyers and sellers.

21:15.370 --> 21:18.700
Exchanges that are at times cutthroat, and at times heartwarming.

21:19.070 --> 21:22.130
Drawing and writing is not all there is to doujinshi.

21:22.370 --> 21:24.310
Distributing it yourself and interacting with your customers...

21:24.310 --> 21:25.970
...are also part of doujinshi.

21:26.310 --> 21:29.180
Yes! The exhibition and spot sale does not end until you go home!

21:29.780 --> 21:30.450
I-I see!

21:30.450 --> 21:31.880
Comrade Kazuki,

21:32.420 --> 21:35.680
I hereby acknowledge you as an up-and-coming doujin author!

21:36.220 --> 21:36.880
Okay...

21:37.650 --> 21:39.660
All roads lead to Rome.

21:39.660 --> 21:42.030
Even a thousand-league journey starts with just one step.

21:42.030 --> 21:42.860
Behold!

21:43.160 --> 21:45.290
That is the star of doujin!

22:20.160 --> 22:24.400
<i>The distant sky looked bright...</i>
<i>Touku no Sora ga Akaruku Mieta</i>

22:24.400 --> 22:28.900
<i>...and we began walking.</i>
<i>Soshite Bokura wa Arukihajimeta</i>

22:29.010 --> 22:33.410
<i>Getting our feet caught in the mud.</i>
<i>Nukarumi ni Ashi o Torarenagara</i>

22:33.580 --> 22:37.480
<i>Heading for a shapeless city.</i>
<i>Katachi no Nai Machi o Mezashite</i>

22:37.480 --> 22:41.620
<i>The pocket in my heart was full...</i>
<i>Kokoro no Naka no Pocket ni wa</i>

22:41.620 --> 22:45.890
<i>...of the grownup things we'd just learned.</i>
<i>Oboetate no Otona ga Ippai</i>

22:46.060 --> 22:50.460
<i>Having taken off our uniforms...</i>
<i>Seifuku o Nuida Bokura ni wa</i>

22:50.590 --> 22:54.630
<i>... the wind was just a little too cold.</i>
<i>Kaze wa Sukoshi Tsumetasugita</i>

22:54.630 --> 22:58.170
<i>Who in the world am I?</i>
<i>Ittai Boku wa Dare Darou</i>

22:58.170 --> 23:03.110
<i>I think about that every so often.</i>
<i>Tokidoki Sonna Koto o Omou</i>

23:03.240 --> 23:06.740
<i>In the world outside the school building...</i>
<i>Kousha no Soto no Sekai de wa</i>

23:06.740 --> 23:12.180
<i>...it's like everyone is a</i> <i>pawn in a game of chess.</i>
<i>Daremo ga Marude Chess no Koma sa</i>

23:13.250 --> 23:17.690
<i>I'm here for you.</i>
<i>Kimi no Tame ni Boku ga Ite</i>

23:17.690 --> 23:21.730
<i>And you for me.</i>
<i>Boku no Tame ni Kimiga</i>

23:21.730 --> 23:26.260
<i>When you think about that...</i>
<i>Sou Omoeba Daremo ga</i>

23:26.260 --> 23:35.230
<i>... everyone is needed by someone.</i>
<i>Dareka no Tame ni Hitsuyou sa</i>

23:55.860 --> 24:20.050
PREVIEW

23:58.630 --> 24:02.400
Hey, Kazuki, what's this about suddenly doing a next episode preview?

24:02.400 --> 24:06.670
Well, Taishi just talks such nonsense, so we fired him.

24:06.670 --> 24:07.740
I see.

24:07.740 --> 24:09.610
But, hey, the camera's already rolling.

24:09.610 --> 24:12.940
What? Oh, you're kidding!
Um, um, um, next time is...

24:12.940 --> 24:15.850
Next time is "We Really
Have No Money!"

24:15.850 --> 24:17.880
Taishi, when in the world did you...

24:17.880 --> 24:20.350
Set your channels!

24:20.420 --> 24:22.050
No, no, no!

24:20.720 --> 24:26.250
NEXT TIME

24:20.720 --> 24:26.250
WE REALLY

24:20.720 --> 24:26.250
HAVE NO MONEY!
